{
  "_comment": [
    "Canonical skeletons, one per rig_type. Anatomy comes from the RECOGNISED CLASS, not",
    "from guessing at the player's strokes -- that guessing is what made drawn creatures",
    "tear, weld and animate the wrong parts.",
    "",
    "pivot/tip are fractions of the drawing's bounding box: [0,0] is its top-left corner,",
    "[1,1] its bottom-right. So the skeleton stretches to whatever the player drew.",
    "influence is a falloff radius as a fraction of the bbox diagonal; the root bone uses 0",
    "to mean UNBOUNDED, which is what guarantees every ink point has some bone to follow.",
    "capture softly biases which region of ink a bone claims -- it never cuts anything.",
    "amplitude_key / frequency_key name a field in game/config/rigs/<id>.json, so per-species",
    "tuning lives with the species instead of hardcoded in GDScript.",
    "states scales the amplitude per motion state; a missing state means the bone holds rest.",
    "",
    "An entity may add a \"skeleton\" block to its own rigs/<id>.json; bones merge BY NAME",
    "over the archetype (add, override, or {\"remove\": true})."
  ],
